	(text "S17.2: the light turns on within 0.5 s of the lid opening and off within 2 s of it closing. Off-board WS2812B strip, up to 16 LEDs;\nfirmware caps its draw at 0.5 A. Power: +5V_AUX through F12 (1.5 A PTC, same part as the AUX ports), so the light is only powered\nwhile the Pi is up. Off-board: put a 470-1000 uF / 10 V electrolytic across the strip power at the strip end.\nData: PB5 = SPI1_MOSI (AF0), TX-only master with DMA, 6 MHz (48 MHz / 8); one SPI byte per WS2812 bit (0 -> 0xC0, 1 -> 0xF0);\nend each frame with at least 300 us of zeros. SPI1 SCK is not mapped to a pin. Fallback: TIM16_CH1 on PB8 (AF2) + DMA (schematic change).\nU14 (SN74LV1T125, VIH 2.03 V at VCC = 5 V) lifts the 3.3 V data to 5 V: WS2812B needs VIH >= 0.7 x VDD = 3.5 V.\nIts input has no clamp diode to VCC (SCLS745D Fig. 8-2, VI max 7 V, II +/-1 uA at VCC = 0 V), so PB5 may drive it while +5V_AUX is off.\nR59 holds the data low while the MCU resets. R60 damps the cable; D16 is ESD protection at J24.\nInterlock: firmware turns the light off whenever the latch servo moves (keeps the worst-case input at 8.4 A; see fuse-selection.md).\nJ24 (JST XH, top entry): 1 = +5 V (LIGHT_5V), 2 = DIN, 3 = GND. Layout: U14, R60, D16, C55, C56 and F12 at J24, on the payload-side edge."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2f1dc406-f980-405e-bf14-e8ebb7c83b2e")
	)
